<%# The debate transcript — the pinned Turbo-Stream target that new turns append to
    (debate_turns/create.turbo_stream.erb) and that Increment 2b broadcasting reuses
    untouched. Locals: debate, turns (eager-loaded, ordered by position).

    DESIGN SYSTEM (Slice 9, Task 4.5) — DebateTurn.prompt.md: "Turns alternate between
    the two participants and stack with 4px gaps." A transcript is the one stack in the
    product that is TIGHTER than the 8px cards-on-a-page rhythm of Card.prompt.md,
    because the rows are one exchange rather than unrelated feed items — so `gap-1`,
    not `gap-2`. It stays a plain flex stack: no wrapper card, no divider, no border.
    Nesting a card here would give the transcript edges of its own, which is exactly
    what Card.prompt.md's "internal sections are separated by a hairline, not by extra
    shadow" rules out. %>
<div id="<%= dom_id(debate, :transcript) %>" class="debate-transcript flex flex-col gap-1 my-4">
  <%= render partial: "debates/debate_turn", collection: turns, as: :debate_turn, locals: {debate: debate} %>
</div>
